The '''Confederal Congress''' ({{lang-bl|Congreso Confederales}}) represents the "highest form of democratic authority" within the political system of the [[Balisca|Baliscan Confederation]]. It brings together delegates from across the confederation, where they discuss the issues at hand and take their decisions back with them to local {{W|popular assemblies}}. The current [[Secretary General of Balisca|Secretary General]] elected by the Congress is [[Zavier Bilal]]. The Congress must convene at least twelve times a year.

The Congress operates on the basis of {{W|consensus democracy|consensus}} and [[W:Delibriative democracy|deliberation]], and it is officially {{W|Nonpartisanism|non-partisan}}. There are no [[W:Political parties|political parties]], although temporary coalitions tend to form issue by issue based on a member's philosophy of government, geographic background, and constituency.

The Congress is composed of delegates (currently numbering 736), each of whom represents a [[commune district]], or an [[autonomous commune]]. Delegates are elected for five year terms, and are constitutionally limited to two terms. Per the 2022 Constitution of Balisca, any adult 18 years of age or older can become elected in any public election. Specifically, to be a candidate in the Confederal Congress the person has to reach this age during the time for which the elections are held. Therefore, the minimum age to be a candidate is 14 years (plus or minus a few days, depending on the date of the next elections).
==Functions of the Congress==
Its purpose is to coordinate policies and initiatives that require cooperation among communities, such as confederal infrastructure projects, disaster response, or international diplomacy. It also facilitates the sharing of resources and expertise between communities to address collective challenges.

The Congress operates via {{W|consensus-based decision-making}} to reach agreements on confederal matters. Each delegate would participate in discussions, and proposals would be refined until a broad consensus is achieved. As with all institutions of authority in Balisca, power within the congress is [[W:Horizontalidad|horizontal]], ensuring that each delegate and their district is able to [[W:Participatory democracy|participate]]. Delegates serving in the Congress are bounded to their electorate and subject to immediate recall, meaning that their decisions must align with the directives from their communities, and they can be replaced if they fail to represent their communities effectively.
