==Elections==
===Eligibility requirements===
According to the Constitution, delegates are the representatives of their commune, canton, or region. To be a delegate, for any of the two principles of choice, you must meet the following requirements:
*Being a Balisca citizen, either by birth or naturalization, in the exercise of their rights.
*Be eighteen years of age or older on election day.
*Being from the region in the election, or resident with an effective residence of more than six months prior to the date of the election.
*Not being active duty in the defense forces or have control of rural guard at least ninety days before the election.
*Not be a secretary or under secretary of state unless it is definitively separated from office at least ninety days before the election.
*Not be reconciliator of any court (to include communal courts) unless definitively separated from office six months before the election.
*Not exceeding the age of 55 before or during the election (age 60 is mandatory retirement from the Confederal Congress)
===Elections===
The [[Constitution of Balisca]] establishes that the deputies are chosen by [[w:Universal suffrage|universal]], free, [[w:Equal suffrage|equal]], [[w:Direct suffrage|direct]] and [[w:Secret suffrage|secret suffrage]]. The election is held every three years or before in case of a [[w:Snap election|snap election]]. The members of the Congress are elected by [[W:Instant-runoff voting|instant-runoff voting]] in each [[commune district]].

